WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:07.990
Another day, another failed attempt to execute
SCP-682 - The infamous Hard To Destroy Reptile.

00:00:07.990 --> 00:00:13.900
The most recent attempt was SCP-272, an Old
Iron Nail with the ability to pin people’s

00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:18.060
shadows to the ground and tear them to shreds
when different configurations of light make

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:20.090
their shadows go haywire.

00:00:20.090 --> 00:00:24.949
Just when it seemed like 272 and a high-powered
disco ball might be the thing to win the Foundation’s

00:00:24.949 --> 00:00:30.540
war against the misanthropic lizard, it did
what it always did: Pulled out a trump card,

00:00:30.540 --> 00:00:32.290
and ruined everything.

00:00:32.290 --> 00:00:37.370
Its body evolved a sudden, intense bioluminescence
that completely eliminated the beast’s shadow

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:40.530
by overpowering all other light sources in
the room.

00:00:40.530 --> 00:00:44.570
This not only rendered the Foundation’s
strobe lights utterly useless, but blinded

00:00:44.570 --> 00:00:49.399
several members of D-Class personnel who were
sent in to check on the beast during testing.

00:00:49.399 --> 00:00:54.520
This resulted, predictably, in another Big,
Fat L for the SCP Foundation.

00:00:54.520 --> 00:00:57.910
682: 435, Foundation: 0.

00:00:57.910 --> 00:01:01.550
And nobody was more frustrated by this than
Dr. Samet.

00:01:01.550 --> 00:01:04.720
Samet was a Foundation greenhorn with big
ambitions.

00:01:04.720 --> 00:01:08.609
Like every jerk at the office, he was less
concerned with doing his job right, and far

00:01:08.609 --> 00:01:11.159
more concerned with climbing the corporate
ladder.

00:01:11.159 --> 00:01:15.490
Samet had done all he could to cozy up to
Site Directors and even the Overseers far

00:01:15.490 --> 00:01:20.049
above, all with the goal of someday getting
a seat at their high table.

00:01:20.049 --> 00:01:25.329
But as any SCP fans know, they’re not just
giving out positions on or just under the

00:01:25.329 --> 00:01:26.499
O5 Council.

00:01:26.499 --> 00:01:29.860
To swing something like that, you need to
really make an impression.

00:01:29.860 --> 00:01:31.280
You need to wow them.

00:01:31.280 --> 00:01:34.990
And what would be a better way to do that
than being the person who killed SCP-682?

00:01:34.990 --> 00:01:41.259
Surely, if he actually buried that beast,
they’d hand him the keys to the proverbial

00:01:41.259 --> 00:01:42.259
castle.

00:01:42.259 --> 00:01:47.569
So Dr. Samet had done everything he could
to get reassigned to the 682 termination effort,

00:01:47.569 --> 00:01:52.209
and only now was he realizing just how in
over his head he truly was.

00:01:52.209 --> 00:01:54.929
Dr. Samet needed help from a higher power.

00:01:54.929 --> 00:02:00.119
If he even hoped of beating SCP-682, the man
needed God on his side.

00:02:00.119 --> 00:02:03.740
Thankfully, they just so happened to have
God chilling out in his containment cell in

00:02:03.740 --> 00:02:04.810
Site 17.

00:02:04.810 --> 00:02:09.569
Perhaps, through enlisting the help of earth’s
divine arbiter, he could bring an end to the

00:02:09.569 --> 00:02:14.689
scourge of SCP-682 and rocket himself to success
in the process.

00:02:14.689 --> 00:02:19.569
However, while Dr. Samet may have been arrogant,
he wasn’t completely delusional.

00:02:19.569 --> 00:02:24.100
He knew that he didn’t have the standing
to address SCP-343 directly, much less to

00:02:24.100 --> 00:02:27.420
ask him for a hand in destroying SCP-682.

00:02:27.420 --> 00:02:30.250
He’d need a go-between.

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:35.650
Someone with tenure, someone who commanded
respect among SCP Foundation staff as well

00:02:35.650 --> 00:02:37.930
as the very anomalies they governed.

00:02:37.930 --> 00:02:41.660
Perhaps someone who was a little bit anomalous
themselves…

00:02:41.660 --> 00:02:46.379
And who better fits this description than
the living legend, Dr. Jack Bright?

00:02:46.379 --> 00:02:50.320
Dr. Samet had, of course, read the doctor’s
personnel files.

00:02:50.320 --> 00:02:54.159
Everybody at the Foundation knew about Dr.
Bright’s exploits - From what he’s done,

00:02:54.159 --> 00:02:58.370
to the various things he isn’t allowed to
do, which we’ll cover in a future video.

00:02:58.370 --> 00:03:04.379
He also dug up the SCP-963 files: The anomalous
medallion keeping Dr. Bright alive, whether

00:03:04.379 --> 00:03:05.790
he likes it or not.

00:03:05.790 --> 00:03:09.791
While a discussion of the exact nature of
the medallion isn’t something you’d want

00:03:09.791 --> 00:03:14.890
to have in front of Dr. Bright himself - After
all, it’s a touchy subject - you could make

00:03:14.890 --> 00:03:17.749
the argument that the medallion is the real
him.

00:03:17.749 --> 00:03:22.090
It’s where his soul is condemned to spend
perhaps the rest of eternity, killing and

00:03:22.090 --> 00:03:25.400
stealing the body of anyone or anything that
touched it.

00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:30.090
He’d become an immortal parasite, destined
to take the finite lives of others while his

00:03:30.090 --> 00:03:31.989
own marches on forever.

00:03:31.989 --> 00:03:33.090
Remind you of anyone?

00:03:33.090 --> 00:03:38.340
Dr. Samet got into contact with Dr. Bright
and explained his plan: With Bright’s help,

00:03:38.340 --> 00:03:44.219
he’d recruit SCP-343, and bring the very
wrath of God down onto the Hard to Destroy

00:03:44.219 --> 00:03:45.219
Reptile.

00:03:45.219 --> 00:03:49.410
Of course, while Dr. Samet naturally assumed
himself to be the smartest person in the room,

00:03:49.410 --> 00:03:54.060
Dr. Bright had a more realistic assessment
of the ambitious young turk’s skills.

00:03:54.060 --> 00:04:00.389
He saw Samet for what he truly was: A climber,
a buttkisser, a greedy, power-hungry bureaucrat

00:04:00.389 --> 00:04:04.239
wearing a lab coat, and he thought that made
him a researcher?

00:04:04.239 --> 00:04:05.420
It was laughable.

00:04:05.420 --> 00:04:10.219
What Dr. Bright found less funny, though,
was Dr. Samet’s insistence on calling him

00:04:10.219 --> 00:04:11.709
“SCP-963.”

00:04:11.709 --> 00:04:16.650
There’s a lot to know about Dr. Bright,
but one thing you should definitely commit

00:04:16.650 --> 00:04:23.810
to memory is that you should never, under
any circumstances, call Dr. Bright SCP-963.

00:04:23.810 --> 00:04:27.840
And if you were forever entwined with a necklace
that doomed you to watch everyone you know

00:04:27.840 --> 00:04:32.960
and love age and die, while depriving you
of that same release, you’d probably resent

00:04:32.960 --> 00:04:34.880
being associated with it, too.

00:04:34.880 --> 00:04:39.210
Dr. Bright did agree to participate in Dr.
Samet’s harebrained termination scheme,

00:04:39.210 --> 00:04:45.330
but with a warning that he did not give lightly:
If ever Dr. Samet called him 963 again, he

00:04:45.330 --> 00:04:49.380
would have one of his own loyal team members
- nicknamed The Lucky Bunch, for their high

00:04:49.380 --> 00:04:54.560
survival rate compared to other Foundation
research teams - shoot him in the foot.

00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:58.930
Dr. Bright steeled himself and entered 343’s
containment cell, where the playful deity

00:04:58.930 --> 00:05:03.870
had taken the form of the late comedian George
Burns, complete with his trademark glasses

00:05:03.870 --> 00:05:05.449
and half-smoked stogy.

00:05:05.449 --> 00:05:10.639
They made small talk, with 343 delivering
his usual high-handed, cryptic parables about

00:05:10.639 --> 00:05:13.300
his plans for Dr. Bright, and everybody else.

00:05:13.300 --> 00:05:17.400
He even momentarily teased the idea of freeing
him from his curse.

00:05:17.400 --> 00:05:20.470
But Dr. Bright knew better than to buy into
these fairy tales.

00:05:20.470 --> 00:05:26.970
He talked SCP-343 into a cross test, but didn’t
tell him that it was with 682, or that he

00:05:26.970 --> 00:05:29.090
was expected to terminate it.

00:05:29.090 --> 00:05:31.250
That was better left as a surprise.

00:05:31.250 --> 00:05:36.129
Dr. Samet and Dr. Bright stood in the observation
area outside the cross-testing chamber.

00:05:36.129 --> 00:05:39.800
Samet was giddy with excitement and confidence
in this new experiment.

00:05:39.800 --> 00:05:42.889
Dr. Bright’s reactions were a hell of a
lot more measured.

00:05:42.889 --> 00:05:48.069
He’d been working at the Foundation long
enough now to know that terminating SCP-682

00:05:48.069 --> 00:05:49.520
was a fool’s errand.

00:05:49.520 --> 00:05:54.729
The only researchers still intent on trying
it were doing so out of stubbornness and ego.

00:05:54.729 --> 00:05:59.720
And when 343 and 682 were released into the
chamber, Dr. Bright’s healthy pessimism

00:05:59.720 --> 00:06:01.460
was more than justified.

00:06:01.460 --> 00:06:06.430
682 attacked a nearby door, attempting to
breach containment, while 343 looked around,

00:06:06.430 --> 00:06:09.250
confused and seemingly unable to see anything.

00:06:09.250 --> 00:06:13.840
When he was ordered to kill 682, he was shocked
to learn 682 was even in the room.

00:06:13.840 --> 00:06:18.150
He stormed off moments later in a huff, saying,
“He's not one of mine.

00:06:18.150 --> 00:06:19.780
Deal with him yourself.”

00:06:19.780 --> 00:06:21.560
Dr. Bright was unsurprised.

00:06:21.560 --> 00:06:24.440
Dr. Samet was shocked and furious.

00:06:24.440 --> 00:06:25.820
How could this have failed?

00:06:25.820 --> 00:06:28.129
They literally had God on their side!

00:06:28.129 --> 00:06:32.020
This setback would seriously compromise his
chances of rising through the ranks, unless

00:06:32.020 --> 00:06:36.490
he found a quick way to make the best out
of a bad situation and save face.

00:06:36.490 --> 00:06:39.250
Without even thinking, he turned to Dr. Bright
and said:

00:06:39.250 --> 00:06:40.250
“Fine.

00:06:40.250 --> 00:06:41.250
It didn't work.

00:06:41.250 --> 00:06:42.250
Doesn't matter.

00:06:42.250 --> 00:06:43.470
Get yourself ready 963, you're going in.”

00:06:43.470 --> 00:06:45.539
So it was decided.

00:06:45.539 --> 00:06:51.240
Dr. Bright himself would face off with SCP-682
in SCP-343’s place.

00:06:51.240 --> 00:06:56.080
Dr. Bright was a betting man, he loved a good
game of chance, and he estimated that his

00:06:56.080 --> 00:06:58.560
odds of succeeding were exceptionally low.

00:06:58.560 --> 00:07:01.000
But what would be the point in refusing?

00:07:01.000 --> 00:07:05.639
Even if he couldn’t kill SCP-682, perhaps
he would get lucky, and the reptile would

00:07:05.639 --> 00:07:06.919
kill him instead.

00:07:06.919 --> 00:07:08.710
So many enticing possibilities.

00:07:08.710 --> 00:07:11.639
Dr. Bright left to prepare for the coming
battle.

00:07:11.639 --> 00:07:16.020
And, because nobody would say that Dr. Bright
wasn’t a man of his word, he had one of

00:07:16.020 --> 00:07:18.539
his assistants shoot Dr. Samet in the foot.

00:07:18.539 --> 00:07:23.039
A few days later, Dr. Bright, Dr. Samet - Now
in a wheelchair while he recovered from his

00:07:23.039 --> 00:07:28.010
unfortunate foot injury - and a collection
of other researchers, including Dr. Sophia

00:07:28.010 --> 00:07:33.110
Light, were convened in a conference room,
planning out their assault on SCP-682.

00:07:33.110 --> 00:07:38.750
A mechanical “staff” of sorts was laying
on the table in front of him, a kind of powerful

00:07:38.750 --> 00:07:42.009
taser capable of firing out painful bolts
of electricity.

00:07:42.009 --> 00:07:47.219
It would be the only object Dr. Bright carried
into the chamber with him that day.

00:07:47.219 --> 00:07:52.199
But only as a way of getting 682’s attention,
not as a weapon.

00:07:52.199 --> 00:07:55.720
The true weapon was SCP-963.

00:07:55.720 --> 00:08:02.729
The plan was simple: SCP-682 would eat Dr.
Bright, and the power of SCP-963 would destroy

00:08:02.729 --> 00:08:04.039
it from within.

00:08:04.039 --> 00:08:09.070
As anyone with an awareness of 963’s anomalous
properties could tell you, for most living

00:08:09.070 --> 00:08:13.509
beings, touching the medallion results in
immediate brain death, followed by the consciousness

00:08:13.509 --> 00:08:16.349
of Dr. Bright inhabiting your mindless body.

00:08:16.349 --> 00:08:21.619
If they could get this phenomenon to work
for SCP-682, perhaps, with Dr. Bright’s

00:08:21.619 --> 00:08:27.340
mind in 682’s body, could they now end the
life of this wretched beast once and for all?

00:08:27.340 --> 00:08:32.830
Like with all matters involving SCP-682 and
Dr. Bright, it was most likely not going to

00:08:32.830 --> 00:08:34.430
be so simple.

00:08:34.430 --> 00:08:39.060
When Dr. Bright entered the test chamber with
682, as Dr. Samet and the others watched from

00:08:39.060 --> 00:08:42.580
the observation room, the results were sudden
and violent.

00:08:42.580 --> 00:08:48.030
Dr. Bright zapped the monster with his electro-staff,
and it came charging for him, a terrible fury

00:08:48.030 --> 00:08:49.710
of teeth and claws.

00:08:49.710 --> 00:08:54.810
Dr. Bright had died so many times, and yet,
he couldn’t even recall many experiences

00:08:54.810 --> 00:08:56.880
more unpleasant than this.

00:08:56.880 --> 00:09:00.520
And as 682’s interior flesh met SCP-963…

00:09:00.520 --> 00:09:05.020
Dr. Bright woke up in the middle of a strange
new place.

00:09:05.020 --> 00:09:10.210
There was a man standing over him that looked
oddly familiar, except for the strange chainmail

00:09:10.210 --> 00:09:11.880
hauberk he was wearing.

00:09:11.880 --> 00:09:16.590
When Dr. Bright found his feet, he recognized
the man: It was a D-Class.

00:09:16.590 --> 00:09:22.380
In fact, the first body he’d ever inhabited
after his soul fused with SCP-963.

00:09:22.380 --> 00:09:23.590
But he wasn’t alone here.

00:09:23.590 --> 00:09:28.470
There were so many people, all of them wearing
the same chainmail, and carrying the same

00:09:28.470 --> 00:09:32.460
electro-staffs that Dr. Bright had carried
into the chamber with him.

00:09:32.460 --> 00:09:38.210
Little by little, he recognized every single
one of the faces: They were all people whose

00:09:38.210 --> 00:09:40.060
bodies he’d taken.

00:09:40.060 --> 00:09:43.130
Whose lives he’d cut short, to further his
own.

00:09:43.130 --> 00:09:49.110
He looked around and saw more bizarre sights:
A grand castle, structured like a deranged

00:09:49.110 --> 00:09:50.470
Escher painting.

00:09:50.470 --> 00:09:57.260
And up above, drowning out the sky, was a
great, reptilian behemoth, like SCP-682 on

00:09:57.260 --> 00:10:00.870
steroids, made entirely from barbecue sauce.

00:10:00.870 --> 00:10:06.930
The D-Class broke the surreal news: None of
this was real, it was a fantasy his mind had

00:10:06.930 --> 00:10:11.560
concocted to help him cope with his consciousness
bonding with SCP-682.

00:10:11.560 --> 00:10:15.960
A more palatable way of perceiving his new
reality.

00:10:15.960 --> 00:10:20.990
And if he ever wanted to get out and be himself
again, he would need to fight and conquer

00:10:20.990 --> 00:10:22.480
the beast within.

00:10:22.480 --> 00:10:27.960
Dr. Bright joined forces with his past victims,
including one former Level 2 Researcher, Damon

00:10:27.960 --> 00:10:28.960
Smith.

00:10:28.960 --> 00:10:34.050
Together, using their electro-staffs, Bright
and his army of mental constructs blasted

00:10:34.050 --> 00:10:37.780
the great monster in the sky from the safe
confines of the castle.

00:10:37.780 --> 00:10:42.030
However, things weren’t quite as safe as
Dr. Bright had first imagined.

00:10:42.030 --> 00:10:46.510
The massive creature descended upon them,
tearing the castle to shreds with its huge

00:10:46.510 --> 00:10:47.510
claws.

00:10:47.510 --> 00:10:50.440
The construct of Damon Smith was devoured
in the process.

00:10:50.440 --> 00:10:56.150
Dr. Bright’s brief illusion of victory was
soon stifled by one immutable fact: You could

00:10:56.150 --> 00:10:58.440
not defeat SCP-682.

00:10:58.440 --> 00:11:03.970
He retreated from the monster into the darkness
of his own nightmares.

00:11:03.970 --> 00:11:05.310
From there, he woke up.

00:11:05.310 --> 00:11:10.781
Dr. Bright was in a hospital bed, the medallion
attached to a new body after 682’s body

00:11:10.781 --> 00:11:12.050
had rejected it.

00:11:12.050 --> 00:11:16.210
He was greeted by Dr. Sophia Light and a member
of the O5 Council.

00:11:16.210 --> 00:11:19.460
Dr. Bright had effectively been gone for days.

00:11:19.460 --> 00:11:24.500
When he asked what happened on the outside,
he was told that 682 had entered a 36-hour

00:11:24.500 --> 00:11:29.570
coma, before growing massive claws and tunneling
out of containment, where it caused a massive

00:11:29.570 --> 00:11:30.570
breach.

00:11:30.570 --> 00:11:35.950
Though strangely, upon breaking out of the
chamber, it only attacked one researcher…

00:11:35.950 --> 00:11:40.870
And in unrelated news, Dr. Samet had been
taken off the 682 case.

00:11:40.870 --> 00:11:45.440
It didn’t take long for things to return
to normal for Dr. Bright - Well, as normal

00:11:45.440 --> 00:11:51.260
as life can be when you’re a man as strange
as him - but while few would notice it, 682

00:11:51.260 --> 00:11:52.620
was left altered.

00:11:52.620 --> 00:11:57.590
It had taken a souvenir from Dr. Bright: Fragments
of the consciousness of Damon Smith.

00:11:57.590 --> 00:12:00.650
It felt his pain, his fear.

00:12:00.650 --> 00:12:04.860
It tasted it, dissected it, and now understood
it.

00:12:04.860 --> 00:12:10.330
And when the opportunity presented itself
once more, as it always did, he couldn’t

00:12:10.330 --> 00:12:13.000
wait to inflict it on others...

00:12:13.000 --> 00:12:19.000
Now go check out “SCP-682 - Ways SCP Foundation
Tried to Kill Hard To Destroy Reptile” and

00:12:19.000 --> 00:12:24.390
“How to Kill SCP-682 - Theories and Ideas”
for more entries in the seemingly endless

00:12:24.390 --> 00:12:27.920
quest to finally put SCP-682 in the ground
for good!

